# Commits that changed formatting and nothing else, so `git blame` can skip them and
# name whoever last changed the LOGIC of a line instead of whoever last ran a linter.
#
# GitHub reads this file automatically in its blame view. Locally it needs
# `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`, which `qb-hooks install`
# sets per checkout — a repo cannot set it for you, and a worktree does not inherit it.
#
# ONLY put a commit here if it changed no behaviour. Anything with a judgement in it
# belongs in blame, and hiding it is worse than the churn: the next reader loses the
# one thing that would have told them a decision was made here. A commit that mixes
# the two should be split rather than listed.

